div.p:
[The late Mr. Jonathan Swift Somers, laureate of Spoon River (
                  see page 111
                  ), planned The Spooniad as an epic in twenty-four books, but unfortunately did not live to complete even the first book. The fragment was found among his papers by William Marion Reedy and was for the first time published in Reedy’s Mirror of December 18th, 1914.]
